add(24,[24,25,74],'unproved claim',[49,54],'54–58;192','Fil¹(p)=Ker F_M=Im V_M; équivalence','Over a perfect characteristic-p ring A, a finite projective Witt Dieudonné module with FV=VF=p has a uniquely determined Hodge submodule after reduction modulo p; classification over perfect rings is a separate input to the proposed route on scan 54.','The displayed kernel/image equality must be read on M modulo p: on a p-torsion-free Witt module F is injective. The notes correctly distinguish this admissibility from Fontaine weak admissibility.','M modulo p is the modern reconstruction suggested by the frozen subscript M_o|0; the transcription alone does not resolve that subscript.')
add(26,[26],'self-flagged step',[49],'60','ne pas fournir un champ','The category obtained by globally tensoring BT Hom groups with Qp need not satisfy descent.','The warning is explicit. On a disjoint union of characteristic-p points, quasi-endomorphisms p^{-n} of the constant height-one étale group have unbounded denominators and cannot glue to an element of (product Zp)[1/p]. This verifies the earlier run’s example.','The disjoint-union counterexample is the earlier run’s construction, independently checked here.')
