add(80,[80,81],'unproved claim',[56,66],'223–232;582','fermés dans X de réunion X','For an excisive closed cover X=X prime union X double-prime, Mayer–Vietoris gives the Euler identity, three-out-of-four finiteness, and finiteness of both pieces when X and their intersection have finite total cohomology.','The stronger bracketed assertion follows degree by degree from exactness. Closedness alone does not imply singular excision, and the final summary also omits the cover hypothesis.')
add(82,[82],'unproved claim',[56,66],'234–244;586–588','dominé homotopiquement','Homotopy domination splits cohomology and preserves its finiteness; homotopy equivalence preserves its Euler number.','The inserted dominé supports only the first implication; the subsequent equivalence supplies equality. A point dominated by a circle shows why the two conclusions differ.')
